{"entries":{"copy|Most respondents discussed how often to take an opioid with the prescriber. Fewer discussed side effects, when to reduce the dose, overdose or addiction. Ask about leftover pills and safe disposal (p289–290).":["u8"],"copy|The poll asked about marijuana’s pain-relief benefits: 31% thought it definitely relieved pain and 38% thought it probably did. These are respondents’ beliefs (p290).":["u25"],"copy|Invite sexual-health discussions. Ask about urinary incontinence: some women do not raise it because they consider it mild or a normal part of aging (p290–292).":["u10"],"copy|Discuss expected health-care costs around retirement. In the poll, 13% of adults aged 50–64 went without medical care because of cost in the prior year. Some postponed retirement to retain employer-sponsored coverage (p294).":["u13"]},"maxId":25,"sequenceOffsets":[[26,-25],[33,-22],[35,-21],[46,0]]}
